WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:07.100
If you are a responsible citizen of the Internet,
then surely you have heard of one Nicolas Cage.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:13.330
"I said, put the bunny back in the box."

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.410
The actor is one of the best of his generation,
an Academy Award winner who makes a great

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.130
film every few years. But in between, he takes
pretty much any gig offered to him, then he

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.340
commits, goddammit, which results in this.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.700
"No, no, not the bees! Not the bees! Aggghhh!"

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:32.129
But Television should get its own Nicolas
Cage, and in the grand tradition of TV, he

00:00:32.129 --> 00:00:39.129
should sort of feel like a department store
knockoff of Cage.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:48.400
Fortunately, we TV fans have just that, and
we’ve had him for years now. His name is

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.230
Dylan McDermott.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.700
He might have been Emmy-nominated for his
work on The Practice, but his true strength?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.280
It’s shouting about things.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.200
"I needed you, and you got a dog!"

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.800
"It was me you should have been curling up with at night!"

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.790
It’s entirely possible McDermott himself
didn’t know he was TV’s Nicolas Cage,

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.170
but as with so many things, Glee co-creator
Ryan Murphy looked deep into McDermott’s

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.990
soul and saw a raving lunatic just waiting
to get out. He made McDermott the male lead

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:17.189
of the first season of American Horror Story,
and a legend was born.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:20.289
"She's having twins, and only one of them
is mine."

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:25.819
"The sad fact is that I'm shooting blanks.
You can ask my ex-wife. We tried for five

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.200
years."
"All it takes is one good swimmer."

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.999
Throughout that season, McDermott gave the
pitch of utter, defeated angst to so many

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:36.740
terrible lines that it became possible to
watch the show entirely to see what he would

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.090
say next.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.259
"You ruined everything!"

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:45.119
Even better: it was never entirely possible
to tell if McDermott was in on the joke or

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:50.349
not, which made his performance seem all the
more bizarre. He returned for an arc in season

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:53.479
two, in which he played the main character’s
murderous offspring.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:54.369
[Screaming]

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:56.590
Sadly, it was a bit of a letdown.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.240
"This is delicate work!"

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.369
He went from Horror Story to CBS’s Hostages,
but he brought with him a strong sense that

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:06.799
what TV needed was frowny faces and random
words being whispered.

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:11.519
"You're gonna kill the President of the United
States, Helen. Otherwise, we will... kill

00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:12.409
your family."

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:17.890
Now, he’s on CBS’s new 'Stalker.' The
show is awful, and it tries too hard to make

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:24.890
him “serious.” But there are flickers
here and there. What new horizons of insanity

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:33.300
will Dylan McDermott open up for us? Only
time will tell.

